<section class="dashboard-panel admin-dashboard-insights" data-campaign-summary data-summary-endpoint="/api/admin/campaign-summary" aria-labelledby="campaign-summary-title">
  <div class="dashboard-panel__header"><div><p class="dashboard-panel__eyebrow">Campaign performance</p><h2 class="dashboard-panel__title" id="campaign-summary-title">Email and social overview</h2><p>Email delivery feedback is reconciled with Resend. Instagram engagement comes from Meta when Insights access is configured.</p></div><button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-campaign-summary-refresh>Refresh stats</button></div>
  <p data-campaign-summary-status role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading campaign totals…</p>
  <div class="grid grid--3 campaign-summary-grid" data-campaign-summary-cards></div>
</section>

<section class="dashboard-panel admin-stats-section admin-dashboard-insights" data-admin-stats-section>
  <div class="dashboard-panel__header"><div><p class="dashboard-panel__eyebrow">Growth metrics</p><h2 class="dashboard-panel__title" id="admin-stats-title">Member and vehicle statistics</h2><p data-admin-stats-description>Loading statistics…</p></div></div>
  <div class="stack" data-admin-stats-container>
    <section aria-labelledby="public-stats-title"><h3 id="public-stats-title">Published on the homepage</h3><p class="form-hint">Public consent-filtered figures — owner joins use contact consent; evidence totals use anonymised-analysis consent.</p><div class="grid grid--4 stat-cards" data-published-stats></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="all-member-stats-title"><h3 id="all-member-stats-title">All member records</h3><p class="form-hint">Private operational totals, including records not included in public evidence.</p><div class="grid grid--4 stat-cards" data-member-stats><article class="stat-card"><h3 class="stat-card__label">Total Members</h3><p class="stat-card__value" data-total-members>—</p></article><article class="stat-card stat-card--accent"><h3 class="stat-card__label">Verified Accounts</h3><p class="stat-card__value" data-verified-count>—</p></article></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="country-table-title"><h3 id="country-table-title">Members by country</h3><p class="form-hint">Join country, then vehicle country, then a recognised UK registration. We do not assume a country where none is recorded.</p><div class="table-wrapper"><table class="data-table" data-country-table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Country</th><th scope="col">Joined</th><th scope="col">Registered</th><th scope="col">Verified</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="member-timeline-title"><h3 id="member-timeline-title">Members joined by day</h3><canvas class="admin-timeline" data-member-timeline width="600" height="300" role="img" aria-label="Daily members joined trend"></canvas></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="verified-timeline-title"><h3 id="verified-timeline-title">Verified accounts by day</h3><canvas class="admin-timeline" data-verified-timeline width="600" height="300" role="img" aria-label="Daily verified accounts trend"></canvas></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="vehicle-section-title"><h3 id="vehicle-section-title">Vehicle statistics</h3><div class="grid grid--4 stat-cards" data-vehicle-stats><article class="stat-card"><h3 class="stat-card__label">Total Vehicles</h3><p class="stat-card__value" data-total-vehicles>—</p></article><article class="stat-card"><h3 class="stat-card__label">SoH Readings</h3><p class="stat-card__value" data-soh-count>—</p></article></div><div class="table-wrapper"><table class="data-table" data-model-year-table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / Year</th><th scope="col">Count</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="service-section-title"><div class="dashboard-panel__header"><div><h3 id="service-section-title">Service event summary</h3><p class="form-hint">Review record types, disputes and provider experience separately. Download all non-deleted service and fault records for private analysis, including provider names, titles and descriptions. Known personal details are redacted; identifying context may remain.</p></div><button class="btn btn--secondary" type="button" data-service-export>Download service CSV</button></div><p class="form-hint" role="status" data-service-export-status></p><div class="grid grid--4 stat-cards" data-service-stats><article class="stat-card"><h3 class="stat-card__label">Service records</h3><p class="stat-card__value" data-stat="totalEvents">—</p></article><article class="stat-card"><h3 class="stat-card__label">With a final-fix date</h3><p class="stat-card__value" data-stat="eventsWithFinalFix">—</p></article></div>
      <h4>Submitted service records by vehicle model year</h4><p class="form-hint">Private, self-selected member records joined to registered vehicles. A car can have multiple records and categories; campaign counts are records tagged H570, H571 or H572, not confirmed module replacements. Missing model years appear as Unknown. These figures are not fleet fault rates.</p><div class="table-wrapper"><table class="data-table" data-service-model-year-table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Model year</th><th scope="col">Registered cars</th><th scope="col">Cars with records</th><th scope="col">All records</th><th scope="col">Faults</th><th scope="col">Repairs</th><th scope="col">Recalls</th><th scope="col">H570–H572 tagged</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
      <h4>Resolution time by record type</h4><p class="form-hint">Days are calculated only where both the event date and final-fix date are present. A same-day fix is 0 days; open records are excluded. The median is usually more representative than the average when a few cases ran for a very long time.</p><div class="table-wrapper"><table class="data-table" data-service-event-type-aggregates><thead><tr><th scope="col">Record type</th><th scope="col">Records</th><th scope="col">With final fix</th><th scope="col">Median days</th><th scope="col">Average days</th><th scope="col">Range</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
      <div data-service-disputes hidden><h4>Recorded dispute outcomes</h4><p class="form-hint">These counts are an additional attribute on service records; they are not service providers or record types.</p><div class="table-wrapper"><table class="data-table" data-service-dispute-table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Dispute outcome</th><th scope="col">Records</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></div>
      <h4>Resolution time by service provider</h4><p class="form-hint">Provider rows use the saved provider ID where available and otherwise group obvious case, punctuation, postcode and Jaguar/JLR wording variants. The 20 providers with the most records are shown; spelling differences can remain in older free-text entries.</p><div class="table-wrapper"><table class="data-table" data-service-provider-aggregates><thead><tr><th scope="col">Service provider</th><th scope="col">Records</th><th scope="col">With final fix</th><th scope="col">Median days</th><th scope="col">Average days</th><th scope="col">Range</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><p class="form-hint">The CSV contains every record and uses month dates and 5,000-mile mileage bands. Preparing it reads service records plus only their related member and vehicle redaction data.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
